i don't know if you guys remember but um  about a year ago there was a movement  that  called itself i guess classical  liberalism  which claimed to be part of some new  center of american politics and in  reality it was a complete and total  ruse what they wanted to do  was to sort of normalize wacky  libertarian conservatism as if it were  the new center of american politics when  it really wasn't the new center of  american politics but  just because that movement was wrong in  identifying a new center  doesn't mean that there isn't an  identifiable new center and that's what  i want to talk about today and i think  the context that will be relevant and  interesting here is that  if we on the left want to keep  moving ourselves to the left as a  country  we want to understand the areas in which  the  average of the country would be  liable to side with us rather than to be  pulled further to the right now i  i i don't know if this is necessary but  as a quick disclaimer before we jump  into this  this new center that i'm going to  describe to you these are not  my views i need to i know that if i  don't do this i will have a hundred  messages tomorrow from people saying  david you centrist  shill it is i i know we're not used to  it with donald trump who's  who's unable to do any kind of uh  abstract thinking  but i'm going to describe to you a set  of beliefs that is not mine so  these are not my beliefs i'm to the left  of this new  center uh now that being said let's get  into the details gallup did a very  interesting study which they've done for  20 to 40 years on different issues  and they looked at where is the country  right now  on a variety of different issues and  they've represented  the issues as well as the shift in  opinion  visually and we're putting that up on  the screen for our visual audience but  i'm also going to describe it to you and  this lets us build up a sort of picture  of where the middle is right now in  america on a number of issues so let's  go  through the eight issues so on on gun  sales  the center the the average of the  country right now the middle  wants more strict gun sales laws than  those that we've had in the past  the center believes that religion is  fairly important but not  very important the center thinks that  military spending is about right  believes the earth should be prioritized  over the economy  and that immigration law should more or  less stay the same in terms of the  number of immigrants coming into the  united states  the center as of today thinks that the  federal income tax is just about right  they don't think it should be raised but  they don't think it should be lowered  that abortion should be legal sometimes  but not always  and that marijuana should be legalized  so remember this is just  an average of the middle but what's  extremely  interesting about this is that it proves  that the new center  is not libertarian it is not classically  liberal and you really need to look at  the details to understand this new  center as an example  if the new center were merely  libertarian it wouldn't favor stricter  gun laws  for example it wouldn't favor  prioritizing the earth over the economy  because that is code for  we've got to regulate business activity  if the center  were libertarian it wouldn't think  immigration laws were just about right  because true libertarians want total  mobility of labor and that's not what we  currently have  what's also important to understand  about  how we came to this new center is how  opinion on these eight issues has  shifted over time so  again looking at one example in the  early 90s  much of the gun laws should be made more  strict  that changed until 2010 when people  wanted looser and looser gun laws  and then since 2010 we've seen a  reversal  which has very strongly returned to the  early 90s numbers where  the center wants stricter gun laws so  does the left as well  religion has been much more steady in  its change over time the center of  america  has found religion less and less  important over time where it now finds  it  fairly but not very important military  spending  has moved pretty erratically often in  concert with what's going on  militarily at the time and then  interestingly if you look at the trends  on immigration  it is very steady over the last 40 years  that immigration to the united states  should should generally speaking be  increased  ending up sort of at its okay where it  is  and then probably not surprisingly on  marijuana  it's been a steady increase in the  proportion of americans that believe  cannabis should be legalized so  why do we care about this again if we  want to build the left  we must understand where the center is  if we misunderstand where the center is  we are not going to properly structure  our platform the center is not  some small government pro-business  conservative the way we would sometimes  be  be uh convinced mitt romney  is not the center mitt romney is far  more reasonable than donald trump  mitt romney is far less offensive and  dangerous than donald trump but mitt  romney is not the center and that's  important to understand  when the left thinks the center is  something that it's not  it tries to appeal to the center in the  wrong ways  so let me know what you think i think  that this new center  represents a lot of the changes we've  been following in the united states  which would include  a sort of status quo perspective on some  issues and a progressivization  on other issues let me know what you  think let me know importantly  how you think our understanding of this  new center could be used  to bring more people to us to our side  and to really push  progressive change
 

